Base: upstream commit dd82ecc6 (2017-08-09, "ignoreKeyProperties additions"),
the commit that added nuget/DapperExtensions.1.6.3.nupkg. Upstream never tagged
1.6.3; this fork tags that commit as `upstream-1.6.3`.

Digital DJ Pool's changes, all build and packaging only. No upstream source
file (*.cs) was modified:

  1. Added DigitalDJPool.DapperExtensions/DigitalDJPool.DapperExtensions.csproj,
     an SDK-style project that compiles the unmodified sources in
     DapperExtensions/ plus DapperExtensions.Net45/DapperAsync*.cs (the async
     API that shipped in the upstream lib/net45 DLL) for net481,
     netstandard2.0 and net10.0. It keeps the assembly name DapperExtensions,
     namespace DapperExtensions and AssemblyVersion 1.6.3.0 (from the upstream
     Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs).
  2. Packaged as NuGet id DigitalDJPool.DapperExtensions 1.6.3, with license
     expression Apache-2.0 and the upstream authors credited.
  3. Changed the Dapper dependency from >= 1.12 (net40/net45) to >= 2.0.30.
     Dapper 2.0.30 is the lowest release with both a net461 and a
     netstandard2.0 build and no known advisory in its dependency graph:
       - 1.50.4 and 1.50.5 have netstandard2.0, but depend on
         System.Data.SqlClient 4.4.0 (GHSA-8g2p-5pqh-5jmc, GHSA-98g6-xh36-x2p7).
       - 2.0.4 has netstandard2.0 only, with no .NET Framework build.
  4. Added framework dependencies: Microsoft.CSharp and System.Data (net481),
     Microsoft.CSharp 4.7.0 (netstandard2.0).
  5. Added global.json (pins .NET SDK 10.0.4xx), NuGet.config (nuget.org only),
     this NOTICE file and a fork section at the top of readme.md.

The upstream net40 target and the legacy projects (DapperExtensions.csproj,
DapperExtensions.Net45.csproj, DapperExtensionsDNXCore, DapperExtensions.sln)
are left as they were and are not used by this build.
